    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0653" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2474a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-22T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to personal letter to Holder,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d479-f1"/> can you
                    obtain total value of merchandise in prize court and approximate value of
                    American goods therein to date or up to April 1? Cable amounts if possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
